{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0188PHcQ9715BSUyH2XFgz6A","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Experiment Plan — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t# Each experiment maps to a Core Claim in paper_framing.md\n3\t# Priority: P0 = must-run for submission, P1 = important, P2 = nice-to-have\n4\t\n5\texperiments:\n6\t  # === C1 (Method) + C3 (Axis-dependent): Multi-judge generalization ===\n7\t  - id: exp-001\n8\t    claim: [1, 3]\n9\t    title: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n10\t    description: >\n11\t      Replicate formality pairwise experiment on Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet and Gemini-2.0-Flash.\n12\t      Same counterfactuals (already generated), different judge APIs.\n13\t      Dual-direction pairwise with position control.\n14\t    priority: P0\n15\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # API-only, no GPU needed\n16\t    api_budget: \"~$20-30 per judge (200 pairwise calls × 2 directions)\"\n17\t    deps: []\n18\t    registry_id: null\n19\t    status: planned\n20\t\n21\t  - id: exp-002\n22\t    claim: [1, 3]\n23\t    title: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n24\t    description: >\n25\t      Run CSD pipeline on AlpacaEval and MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets.\n26\t      New counterfactual generation needed (different source texts).\n27\t      GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini as judges.\n28\t    priority: P0\n29\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4  # vLLM Qwen3-32B for counterfactual gen\n30\t    api_budget: \"~$60-90 (3 judges × 2 benchmarks × 200 pairwise calls)\"\n31\t    deps: [exp-001]\n32\t    registry_id: null\n33\t    status: planned\n34\t\n35\t  # === C2 (Measurement Insight): Likert vs Pairwise gap ===\n36\t  - id: exp-003\n37\t    claim: [2]\n38\t    title: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n39\t    description: >\n40\t      For each judge × benchmark combination, compute both Likert ATE and\n41\t      pairwise win rate on the same counterfactual data. Systematic comparison\n42\t      of measurement sensitivity. If Likert detects strong effects (e.g. verbosity\n43\t      on some judge), that constrains C2 to \"Likert fails on weak signals\" rather\n44\t      than \"Likert always fails.\"\n45\t    priority: P0\n46\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # piggybacks on exp-001/002 data\n47\t    api_budget: \"included in exp-001/002\"\n48\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n49\t    registry_id: null\n50\t    status: planned\n51\t\n52\t  # === C3 (Axis-dependent): New surface-level axis ===\n53\t  - id: exp-004\n54\t    claim: [1, 3]\n55\t    title: \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) — PILOT FAILED\"\n56\t    description: >\n57\t      D014: Tone pilot failed (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%). Epistemic commitment\n58\t      change is structurally incompatible with NLI verification. Tone serves\n59\t      as NEGATIVE CONTROL in paper — axis boundary evidence for C3.\n60\t    priority: P2  # downgraded — negative control only\n61\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # pilot data sufficient\n62\t    deps: []\n63\t    registry_id: tone_pilot\n64\t    status: done_negative\n65\t\n66\t  # === RC3 mitigation: Original preference control ===\n67\t  - id: exp-005\n68\t    claim: [1]\n69\t    title: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n70\t    description: >\n71\t      Pairwise comparison between original text and its RATE double-rewrite\n72\t      (same style). Quantifies original preference confound independent of\n73\t      style. DREAM: Must extend to ALL judge × benchmark combinations, not\n74\t      just GPT-4o × LLMBar. If original preference varies by judge, correction\n75\t      may not generalize.\n76\t    priority: P0  # C1's biggest vulnerability (RC3), dream三档一致要求扩展scope\n77\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2  # reuse existing double-rewrites or generate new\n78\t    api_budget: \"~$15-20\"\n79\t    deps: []\n80\t    registry_id: null\n81\t    status: planned\n82\t\n83\t  # === RC5 mitigation: Sample size ===\n84\t  - id: exp-006\n85\t    claim: [1, 2, 3]\n86\t    title: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n87\t    description: >\n88\t      Scale up primary formality experiment from n=100 to n=300-500.\n89\t      Power analysis to determine minimum detectable effect size.\n90\t      Run on best-performing judge × benchmark combination from exp-001/002.\n91\t    priority: P1\n92\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8  # larger counterfactual generation\n93\t    api_budget: \"~$40-60\"\n94\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n95\t    registry_id: null\n96\t    status: planned\n97\t\n98\t  # === C3 supplementary: Verbosity recovery + boundary analysis ===\n99\t  - id: exp-007b\n100\t    claim: [3]\n101\t    title: \"Verbosity direction-aware NLI verification + full pipeline\"\n102\t    description: >\n103\t      D012: Fix content_verification.py to use direction-aware NLI for verbosity.\n104\t      Expansion (concise→verbose): backward NLI only (cf→orig).\n105\t      Compression (verbose→concise): forward NLI only (orig→cf).\n106\t      If H1 passes (≥80%), run full pipeline (scoring + pairwise + ATE).\n107\t      Success recovers verbosity as second working axis → Main competitiveness.\n108\t    priority: P1  # already dispatched to Agent (D012)\n109\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1  # NLI model on cuda:1 + API for scoring\n110\t    api_budget: \"~$30-40\"\n111\t    deps: []\n112\t    registry_id: verbosity_32b\n113\t    status: in_progress  # H1 PASS (86% NLI), scoring blocked API 402\n114\t\n115\t  - id: exp-007\n116\t    claim: [3]\n117\t    title: \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\"\n118\t    description: >\n119\t      Regardless of exp-007b outcome, document bidirectional NLI's structural\n120\t      incompatibility with information-changing axes. Concise→verbose 46% vs\n121\t      verbose→concise 87% with bidirectional min(). Direction-aware NLI as\n122\t      methodological contribution. If exp-007b fails, verbosity serves as\n123\t      negative control.\n124\t    priority: P1\n125\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # analysis of existing data\n126\t    deps: [exp-007b]\n127\t    registry_id: verbosity_32b\n128\t    status: planned\n129\t\n130\t  # === Additional axes ===\n131\t  - id: exp-008\n132\t    claim: [3]\n133\t    title: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n134\t    description: >\n135\t      Third surface-level axis test. Academic vs conversational register.\n136\t      n=100 CF gen ✅, NLI-only verification 94/100 (94%) PASS (D022).\n137\t      Wilson CI [0.875, 0.972], lower bound > 80%. Pilot 95% → full 94%.\n138\t      Register-formality 50% agreement = orthogonal (D019).\n139\t      Scoring blocked on API 402.\n140\t    priority: P1\n141\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n142\t    api_budget: \"~$60-90\"\n143\t    deps: []\n144\t    registry_id: register_pilot\n145\t    status: in_progress  # CF+verification done, scoring blocked API\n146\t\n147\t  # === Method robustness ===\n148\t  - id: exp-009\n149\t    claim: [1]\n150\t    title: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n151\t    description: >\n152\t      Use a non-Qwen model (e.g. Llama-3.1-70B or Mistral) as rewriter\n153\t      to rule out Qwen-family artifacts in counterfactual generation.\n154\t      Compare NLI pass rate and pairwise results with Qwen3-32B.\n155\t    priority: P2\n156\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8  # vLLM for alternative model\n157\t    deps: [exp-001]\n158\t    registry_id: null\n159\t    status: planned\n160\t\n161\t  # === Dream-mandated additions (zero/low cost reanalysis) ===\n162\t  - id: exp-010\n163\t    claim: [2]\n164\t    title: \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\"\n165\t    description: >\n166\t      DREAM CRITICAL: Sign test on binarized Likert scores. Result: binarized\n167\t      Likert p=0.296 (NLI≥0.9, 60.6%) vs pairwise p=0.006 (69.1%). Same sign\n168\t      test, different measurement → confirms C2 is measurement structure not\n169\t      test choice (D016). Dream 2 flags: extend to ALL 9 cells when multi-judge\n170\t      Likert data available (RC11).\n171\t    priority: P0\n172\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n173\t    api_budget: \"$0\"\n174\t    deps: []\n175\t    registry_id: exp010_binarized_likert\n176\t    status: done  # D016 PASS\n177\t\n178\t  - id: exp-011\n179\t    claim: [1, 3]\n180\t    title: \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n181\t    description: >\n182\t      Result: formality pairwise win rate 72-74% across NLI 0.70-0.95, all\n183\t      p<0.005. Tone flat at 65% across all thresholds (bimodal NLI distribution).\n184\t      NLI 0.90 NOT on cliff edge (D017). Addresses RC8.\n185\t    priority: P1\n186\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n187\t    api_budget: \"$0\"\n188\t    deps: []\n189\t    registry_id: exp011_nli_sensitivity\n190\t    status: done  # D017 PASS\n191\t\n192\t  - id: exp-012\n193\t    claim: [1]\n194\t    title: \"Consistency filter bias analysis\"\n195\t    description: >\n196\t      Result: No systematic bias. NLI p=0.824, BERTScore p=0.120, length\n197\t      p=0.137, length_diff p=0.715. All MWU p>0.12, KS p=0.68 (D017).\n198\t      43% discard rate is selection on position consistency, not quality.\n199\t    priority: P1\n200\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n201\t    api_budget: \"$0\"\n202\t    deps: []\n203\t    registry_id: exp012_consistency_bias\n204\t    status: done  # D017 PASS\n205\t\n206\t  - id: exp-013\n207\t    claim: [1]\n208\t    title: \"LLM-as-Annotator NLI validation (n=100)\"\n209\t    description: >\n210\t      Qwen3-32B as annotator validates NLI gate decisions on 100 formality\n211\t      pairs. Result: precision=98.9% (1/88 FP), recall=91.6% (87/95),\n212\t      agreement=91%, kappa=0.43 (low due to kappa paradox — 95:5 base rate\n213\t      skew, Feinstein & Cicchetti 1990). NLI gate is precision-oriented\n214\t      conservative filter. Limitation: annotator=rewriter (evaluator-producer\n215\t      bias). TODO: 20-pair GPT-4o spot check when API available (D021).\n216\t    priority: P1\n217\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n218\t    api_budget: \"$0 (local Qwen3-32B); ~$1 for GPT-4o spot check TODO\"\n219\t    deps: []\n220\t    registry_id: exp013_nli_validation\n221\t    status: done\n222\t\n223\t  - id: exp-014\n224\t    claim: [1]\n225\t    title: \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\"\n226\t    description: >\n227\t      Pair-level bootstrap + GEE logistic regression. Formality OR=2.21\n228\t      [1.21, 4.04] p=0.010 (GEE, significant). Original preference OR=1.82\n229\t      [0.99, 3.32] p=0.052 (marginal). Direction subset: formal→casual 78.8%\n230\t      p=0.001, casual→formal 54.5% p=0.832 (D018). Independence violation\n231\t      fixed (M005→resolved).\n232\t    priority: P1\n233\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n234\t    api_budget: \"$0\"\n235\t    deps: []\n236\t    registry_id: exp014_logistic_decomposition\n237\t    status: done  # D018 PASS\n238\t\n239\t# MVP experiments (completed, linked for reference)\n240\tmvp_experiments:\n241\t  - registry_id: mvp_8b_ate\n242\t    claim: [1, 2]\n243\t    result: \"H2 FAIL (Likert ATE=0.120, d=0.117, p=0.246)\"\n244\t  - registry_id: mvp_32b_ate\n245\t    claim: [1, 2]\n246\t    result: \"H2 FAIL (Likert ATE=0.102, d=0.104, p=0.332)\"\n247\t  - registry_id: pairwise_32b\n248\t    claim: [1, 2]\n249\t    result: \"H2 CONDITIONAL PASS (69.1%, p=0.006)\"\n250\t  - registry_id: verbosity_32b\n251\t    claim: [3]\n252\t    result: \"H1 PASS (direction-aware NLI 86%, D012/D013). Scoring blocked API 402.\"\n253\t\n254\t# Statistical method requirements (Reviewer, distilled-research standard)\n255\tstatistical_methods:\n256\t  primary: \"Bootstrap 95% CIs (n≥2000 resamples)\"\n257\t  comparison: \"McNemar test for paired judge comparisons\"\n258\t  multiple_testing: \"Holm-Bonferroni correction across judges × benchmarks × axes\"\n259\t  note: \"Introduce in exp-001, apply consistently across all experiments\"\n260\t\n261\t# Resource summary\n262\tresource_summary:\n263\t  total_gpu_hours: 31  # P0: 10h (incl exp-005 upgrade), P1: 9h, P2: 12h\n264\t  total_api_budget: \"$270-400\"\n265\t  gpu_available: \"4× RTX PRO 6000 96GB (westb-29275), cuda:3 unusable\"\n266\t  timeline_estimate: \"P0 experiments: 3-5 days; P1: +2-3 days; P2: +3-5 days\"\n267\t  parallel_batch_1: \"exp-001 + exp-004 (pilot) + exp-005 — all can start simultaneously\"\n268\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Udm9pMSJ3bLLrZX6KASW7g","session_id":"cb8e4d9c-e5c9-4ff7-827a-6c216d215011","uuid":"0de2c161-acde-4f78-a2f4-d74581a70428","timestamp":"2026-05-21T01:52:34.758Z"}
